CQA_530324248359c2f3.answer_pre:
{"answer_pre":"The ST-RIS radar paper explicitly trades off sensing and communication bandwidth: under the constraint B_s+B_c=B_T, increasing B_c (CPM communication bandwidth) necessarily shrinks the chirp bandwidth B_s, degrading ranging Fisher Information (I_tot = a(B_T-B_c)^2 + bB_c^2, with a>>b), so I_tot is monotonically decreasing in B_c — max sensing at B_c=0, max communication at B_c=B_T. Under a sensing-performance constraint Ŝ(β)≥Ŝ_min (β=B_c/B_T), the optimal allocation is derived in closed form as β* = [1−√(1−(1+b/a)(1−Ŝ_min))]/(1+b/a), i.e., the largest bandwidth fraction assignable to communication while still meeting the sensing requirement. This tradeoff exists because the ST-RIS system embeds communication as a phase modulation onto the same physical sensing waveform/spectrum, so sensing and communication literally share and compete for the same finite RF bandwidth B_T.

In contrast, UniFi (the Wi-Fi ISAC paper) claims zero communication overhead because it does not modulate or allocate any dedicated spectrum/bandwidth for sensing at all — it performs sensing purely by passively extracting and reusing CSI already present in normal, irregularly-sampled communication packets (data, management, control frames across multiple bands/PHY formats) without injecting any extra probing packets. Since no additional signal or bandwidth is transmitted for sensing purposes, there is no bandwidth competition and hence no sensing-communication bandwidth tradeoff analogous to the ST-RIS case.

The fundamental architectural difference enabling these divergent paradigms is that the ST-RIS system is a joint waveform-design/backscatter architecture where sensing and communication are two functions carried by the same actively-shaped radar/backscatter signal over a shared bandwidth resource (so allocating spectrum to one necessarily takes it from the other), whereas UniFi's Wi-Fi ISAC architecture is a passive, opportunistic sensing framework that extracts sensing information as a byproduct of pre-existing, independently-generated communication traffic (via a CSI sanitization pipeline and time-aware DNN), meaning sensing consumes no dedicated spectrum and therefore imposes no communication throughput cost.","evidence_pages":[8,9,17,20]}

