{"answer_pre":"In Paper 1, the propagated uncertainty from the spin-orbit coupling parameter λ affects the excitation energies and energy splittings between states but does not change the underlying nuclear configuration or deformation. The λ parameter modifies spin-orbit splitting while preserving the deformation (β₂, γ) structure. In Paper 2, the propagated uncertainty from the low-energy constant M₃ (fitted to the ⁴He charge radius) directly affects the two-body charge density operator, which in turn impacts the spatial charge distribution and consequently the charge radius itself. This represents a structural change in the computed charge distribution. The difference arises because Paper 1's λ governs spin-orbit energy splitting (a spectroscopic effect), while Paper 2's M₃ governs two-body charge density contributions (a structural/spatial effect).","evidence_pages":[3,4,5,14,15,16,17]}
